  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 accuracy. The image modality contributed ~6 points over RNA-only multiprofile, but image-only resnet50 was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image encoder may be underutilized. config_039 isolates a single variable—replacing resnet50 with the stronger imagenet_vit_l—while keeping the proven scvi_n200 encoder, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion. This tests whether a more powerful image representation can further amplify the multimodal gain. It is the highest-upside single-variable extension of the current best, and with only 2 experiments remaining, focusing on the most impactful design axis (image encoder quality) is the best use of this slot."
